<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31129" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nŏmăs</span></b> ,
		ădis, comm., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νομάς</span> (pasturing flocks); in plur.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nŏmădes</span></b> ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>pastoral people
				that wander about with their flocks</i>, 
			<i>Nomads</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 3, 2, §
			22</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In partic., <i>the</i> (wandering) <i>Numidians</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 4,
				320</span></i>; cf. Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				173</span></i> Müll.—In <i>sing.
				collect., a Numidian</i>, <i><span class="en">Sil. 5,
			194</span></i>.—In <i>fem.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nomas versuta,</span>”
				<i>a Numidian fortune-teller</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				4</span></i>
			 (5), 7, 37.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nŏmas</span></b> , ădis,
				f., <i>Numidia</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 8,
				55, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 75,
			8</span></i>.</div>
